 abstract = {This study presents a comprehensive bibliometric and literature survey of research on chroma keying. Chroma keying being a fundamental technique in visual effects and video compositing where the foreground object is separated from a foreground border that is merged with a background border to generate a new combination structure for a unique result [1]–[3]. The process of isolating or extracting a foreground object from its background in an image video is known a matting [4], [5], [3]. In chroma keying the matte is achieved by the application of a solid colour (blue or green) that can be easily distinguished from the foreground subject. In live outdoor sports broadcasts, one of the major challenges lies is applying chroma keying in non consistant or different lighting conditions. The difference in lighting result to different shades of colour in the background to be used. Natural light changes throughout the day, affecting how colours appear on camera. The wide range of colours present in outdoor environments can often lead to blending or overspill effects, where the hues of foreground elements closely resemble those of the background. By analyzing publications from databases such as Scopus and Web of Science, this work identifies key trends, influential authors, research hotspots, and thematic evolutions in chroma keying research. The results provide a quantitative overview and qualitative insights into the progression of chroma keying technologies, algorithms, and applications in film and digital media in the African continent. With these results from the database, different approaches to matting applications have been discovered that can be independent from colour sampling which the author can adopt to address his challenge. Analysis drawn from these data shows that only a certain part of the world has been involved in this study, thus the African continent has a huge gap of research in this area as television productions are on the rise.},
 author = {Gama, Sanele and Sumbwanyambe, Mbuyu and Feukeu, Etienne},
 booktitle = {2025 5th International Multidisciplinary Information Technology and Engineering Conference (IMITEC)},
